      "text": "```python\n\"\"\"\nLRU (Least Recently Used) Cache Implementation\n\nThis module provides a thread-safe LRU cache implementation with O(1) time complexity\nfor both get and put operations.\n\nThread Safety:\n    The LRU cache uses a threading.Lock to ensure thread safety. All public methods\n    (get, put, delete, clear, size) acquire the lock before accessing internal state.\n    This ensures that concurrent access from multiple threads does not corrupt the\n    internal data structures.\n\nComplexity:\n    - get(): O(1) average case\n    - put(): O(1) average case\n    - delete(): O(1) average case\n    - clear(): O(1)\n    - size(): O(1)\n    \n    Space complexity: O(capacity) for storing up to 'capacity' items.\n\nImplementation Details:\n    - Uses a doubly-linked list (via collections.OrderedDict) to maintain access order.\n    - OrderedDict maintains insertion order and allows O(1) move-to-end and pop operations.\n    - When an item is accessed (get) or updated (put), it is moved to the end\n      (most recently used position).\n    - When the",
